# Offline vdW-DF (DRSLL) pin notes — gpw-vdw-df-ice

## Kernel oracle (libvdwxc)

CP2K `VDW_POTENTIAL NON_LOCAL TYPE DRSLL` uses the same Román–Pérez–Soler
kernel family as **libvdwxc DF1**. Hard unit-test pin is libvdwxc 0.5.0 on a
fixed synthetic density (not live in ctest):

```text
# 16^3 cubic L=8 Bohr, rho = exp(-0.5 r^2) blob at center, analytic sigma
E_nl DRSLL/DF1 = 1.2367739353586624e-01 Ha
```

Build pin harness against system libvdwxc (Arrhenius epyc easybuild):

```bash
# module / paths as on 2026-07-25 epyc node
gcc -O2 pin.c -I$LIBVDWXC/include -L$LIBVDWXC/lib -lvdwxc -lfftw3 -lm
```

## Full GPW regression pin

Post-SCF \(E_c^{\mathrm{nl}}\) on Γ-PBE density of the water dimer
(CUTOFF 200 Ry, DZVP-MOLOPT-SR-GTH, 12 Å cell):

```text
E_disp = 1.5194390480303990e-01 Ha
```

## Suggested CP2K twin (when QS + libvdwxc available)

```
&FORCE_EVAL
  METHOD Quickstep
  &DFT
    &XC
      &XC_FUNCTIONAL PBE &END XC_FUNCTIONAL
      &VDW_POTENTIAL
        POTENTIAL_TYPE NON_LOCAL
        &NON_LOCAL
          TYPE DRSLL
          CUTOFF_RC  0.0   ! use default kernel mesh
        &END NON_LOCAL
      &END VDW_POTENTIAL
    &END XC
    &MGRID CUTOFF 200 &END MGRID
    &QS METHOD GPW &END QS
    &SCF  ...  &END SCF
  &END DFT
  &SUBSYS
    ! water dimer geometry as REFERENCE.md
  &END SUBSYS
&END FORCE_EVAL
```

Record `Dispersion energy` / nonlocal XC contribution and CP2K version in
REFERENCE.md when a host provides a fair twin wall.
